# CPT/WPGB Patterns

Use this Rule when writing or reviewing WST Builder Custom Post Type work, including CPT registration, taxonomy setup, ACF CPT field groups, WP Grid Builder card/grid foundations, WST card templates, archive/grid integration, optional single templates, and CPT handoff content.

## Required Context

Before changing CPT, WPGB, ACF, or template structure, read the project-local context and current CPT handoff for:

- CPT naming convention, registered post type, URL slug policy, and detail-page decision.
- Taxonomy decision, hierarchy, public archive behavior, and filtering or label purpose.
- ACF CPT field group approach and field ownership between core post fields, taxonomy, featured image, and ACF.
- WP Grid Builder usage, generated grid/card IDs, display target, and card/grid source.
- Card, archive/grid, carousel/filter, optional single, and optional Section integration template paths.
- Stable selectors, CSS or SCSS paths, target dev or staging URLs, cache command, and handoff storage.

Do not invent real CPT names, rewrite slugs, taxonomy names, ACF keys, field post IDs, WPGB IDs, paths, URLs, selectors, credentials, or client examples. Use placeholders such as `<resource>`, `<url-slug>`, `<field-key>`, `<grid-id>`, `<card-id>`, and `<dev-or-staging-url>` until Project Context or the concrete CPT handoff supplies the real values.

## CPT And Detail-Page Invariants

- Decide whether public detail pages exist before enabling public single URLs, rewrites, archives, search inclusion, or single templates.
- Non-detail CPTs must not accidentally create public single URLs, public archives, or searchable content just because the CPT is visible in the admin.
- Public detail-page CPTs must record URL slug, archive/search behavior, representative single URL, single template path, stable single selector, and local frontend responsibilities in the CPT handoff.
- `show_ui` and `show_in_rest` should be enabled unless the project context gives a reason not to.
- `supports` should include only fields the content model actually uses.

## Taxonomy Invariants

- Add a taxonomy only when it has a clear filtering, grouping, card-label, archive, or editor-organization purpose.
- Taxonomy names usually follow the project pattern, commonly `wso_tax_<resource>`.
- Choose hierarchical behavior deliberately: category-style for controlled groups, tag-style for loose labels.
- Disable public rewrites unless taxonomy archives are part of the brief.
- Record an explicit no-taxonomy decision when the CPT does not need taxonomy.

## ACF CPT Field Invariants

- Prefer core post title, featured image, editor, excerpt, and taxonomy terms before duplicating the same data in ACF fields.
- Create one CPT-specific ACF field group when custom fields are needed, with location rules targeting the registered post type.
- Use project field naming conventions and record generated field keys only after the project creates them.
- Stop when field ownership is unclear; do not invent field names, field keys, or generated IDs.
- Templates must handle optional fields so empty data does not leave broken markup or spacing.

## WP Grid Builder Invariants

- Create WPGB card and grid foundations only when the display target uses WPGB.
- The WPGB grid source should point at the new CPT when the display target is a grid or carousel.
- The WPGB card exists so the grid can select a card; WST PHP card templates may still render the actual markup.
- Record generated grid/card IDs in Project Context or the concrete CPT handoff, never in reusable plugin prose.
- Record an explicit no-WPGB decision when the CPT is rendered only by a custom Section, single template, or another project-specific path.

## Template And Selector Invariants

- Guard PHP templates with `if (! defined('ABSPATH')) exit;`.
- Card templates should expose stable hooks such as `.wso-<resource>-card`.
- Archive, grid, carousel, filter, and optional single templates should expose stable wrapper selectors for frontend QA.
- Public single templates should expose stable hooks such as `.wso-<resource>-single`.
- Preserve selectors used by templates, JavaScript, WPGB behavior, or Playwright checks.
- Minimal server-phase style files may establish hooks, but final spacing, typography, responsive behavior, Chrome Local Overrides spikes, and Playwright checks belong to Frontend Design QA.

## Handoff And Routing Invariants

- Create CPT handoff drafts from `plugins/wst-builder/handoffs/cpt-handoff.template.md` and store filled handoffs at the project-configured CPT handoff storage location.
- Keep CPT handoffs separate from Section handoffs because CPT work has detail-page, taxonomy, WPGB, card, archive/grid, carousel, and optional single-template decisions.
- Completed CPT handoffs route to Frontend Design QA `cpt-frontend-qa` for card, archive/grid, carousel/filter, WPGB output, and optional single-template QA.
- When a CPT display becomes primarily a dedicated WST Section layout, record the split: `frontend-section-qa` owns Section-level layout behavior, while `cpt-frontend-qa` owns CPT card, archive/grid, carousel/filter, and optional single-template behavior.
- Stop instead of guessing when blocking handoff values are unresolved.
